    {'slug': 'selenium-implicit-vs-explicit-wait', 'category': 'selenium', 'title': 'When should you use an explicit wait in Selenium?', 'difficulty': 'Intermediate', 'audience': 'Experienced', 'answer': 'Use an explicit wait when a specific element or state must become ready, such as visibility, clickability, or a text change. It polls until a condition is met or a timeout expires, making synchronization intentional and local to the interaction.', 'example': 'wait.until(EC.element_to_be_clickable((By.CSS_SELECTOR, "button[data-test=save]"))).click()', 'use_case': 'Prefer stable data-test attributes and condition-based waits over fixed sleeps, which slow the suite and still fail intermittently.'},
